  "title": "Chapter 29: Tides and Waves",
  "order": 226,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Tides and waves are two important types of oceanic movements. While waves are primarily generated by wind and affect only the surface layer of water, tides are large-scale periodic rise and fall of sea level caused by gravitational forces of the Moon and the Sun. Both play a critical role in coastal processes, navigation, fisheries, and climate interaction.",
      "id": "u4ap7ti"
    },
